From google/pkcs11test (https://github.com/google/pkcs11test), Apache-2.0,
at the revision pinned in run.sh. The changed lines make the cipher,
signature, MAC and key-pair fixtures, and the five read/write-session tests
that generate a secret key (the latch test and Tookan A3 to A5b), log in
before generating their keys, so they run against this token's
CKF_LOGIN_REQUIRED profile; the context lines below are upstream's. See
README.md for the rationale and for how to regenerate this patch against a
newer revision.

